# RouteMe — Competitive Research & Revenue Strategy

**Date:** 2026-07-25
**Researcher:** Scout
**Context:** Identify competitive advantages and revenue-generating features for RouteMe, a home health nurse routing app.

---

## 1. Competitive Landscape

| Competitor | Position | Strengths | Weaknesses | Pricing |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **WellSky** (Kinnser) | Dominant enterprise EHR | Full vertical integration: EHR+scheduling+billing+payroll. OASIS/ICD-10/claims. CMS-connected. | Monolithic, expensive, long implementation. Basic routing (no turn-by-turn). | $500-$2K+/month |
| **Axxess** | Fast-growing mid-market | Strong mobile-first approach. Offline OASIS. EVV compliance. Real-time claims. | No route optimization. No navigation. Less AI/ML. | $300-$1.5K/month |
| **HHAeXchange** | Provider-payer connectivity | Top-tier EVV compliance. Bi-directional provider-payer. State Medicaid preferred. | Limited clinical docs (no OASIS/SOAP depth). No routing. Aging UI. | $200-$800/month |
| **AlayaCare** | Cloud home health platform | Cloud-native, modern. Basic route optimization. Patient portal. Telehealth. | Route optimization basic. Missing weather/3D/AI. Not best-in-class anywhere. | $400-$2K/month |
| **Canvas Medical** | AI-powered EHR | AI Agents for workflows. API-first. Custom EMRs. | Not home-health specific. No routing, EVV, or OASIS. | Custom |
| **HomeCare HomeBase** | Enterprise giant | Deep EHR/billing/payroll. Robust reporting. Large installed base. | Expensive, complex, dated UI. No modern routing/nav. | $2K-$10K+/month |

**Key Insight:** RouteMe is **10x ahead on routing** — no competitor offers anything close. The fastest path to revenue is layering clinical + billing + compliance features on this routing moat.

