## 3. Top 5 Revenue Features (Ranked)

### 🥇 #1: AI Voice-to-Text SOAP Notes
**Why:** SOAP notes are the #1 time-sink for nurses (5-15 notes/day, 5-10 min each = 30-150 min/day per nurse).

**Implementation:**
- Voice recording → Whisper/Deepgram API → LLM (Claude/GPT-4) → structured SOAP (Subjective, Objective, Assessment, Plan)
- Auto-populate patient demographics, conditions, meds, visit history
- ICD-10 code suggestions from note content
- Offline recording + sync
- Patient signature capture

**Revenue:** $200-500/month per agency as premium add-on. Per-note: $0.10-0.25 (10K notes = $1K-$2.5K)

**Moat:** No competitor offers voice-to-text SOAP integrated with routing. The note is tied to the visit, client, and route automatically.

### 🥇 #2: Billing / Revenue Cycle Management
**Why:** Agencies lose 5-15% of revenue to billing errors, denied claims, slow reimbursement.

**Implementation:**
- Auto-generate claims from visit data (times, location, mileage already tracked)
- Real-time insurance eligibility verification
- Clearinghouse connection (Change Healthcare, Waystar, ZirMed)
- Denial management dashboard with auto-appeals
- Medicare/Medicaid compliance

**Revenue:** $500-1,500/month per agency. Per-claim: $0.50-$1.00. Or 1-3% of collections.

### 🥉 #3: EVV (Electronic Visit Verification) Compliance
**Why:** Mandatory by federal law (21st Century CURES Act). Agencies cannot operate without it.

**Implementation:** Geo-fence clock-in/out (RouteMe already has GPS + timestamps). Patient signature capture. CMS-compliant EVV data export. Telephony fallback.

**Revenue:** $100-300/month per agency. 100% attach rate (mandatory). Already have the data — just need UI + export.

### #4: EHR/EMR Integration
**Why:** Agencies use 3-5 systems. Eliminating dual-entry is the #1 workflow value.

**Implementation:** FHIR R4 API. Bi-directional sync (pull patients/schedules, push visits/mileage/SOAP/EVV). CSV fallback for small agencies. Webhook triggers.

**Revenue:** $300-800/month per agency. $500-$2,500 one-time integration fee.

### #5: OASIS Documentation
**Why:** Required for all Medicare-certified agencies. Complex and drives PDGM reimbursement.

**Implementation:** Mobile OASIS-E forms with skip logic. PDGM payment auto-calculation. LUPA alerts. Pre-claim validation.

**Revenue:** $400-800/month per agency. Or $5-$15 per assessment.

